From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrzej Wilczynski <andrzej.wilczynski@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:27:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net/ice: fix shared PHC timer writes from non-owner port

All ports of a device share one PHC source timer. Only the PCI
function with func_caps.ts_func_info.src_tmr_owned may start, stop or
initialize it. When that function stays on the kernel ice driver, the
kernel keeps the timer running for every port, including the ports
bound to DPDK.

ice_timesync_disable() cleared GLTSYN_ENA.TSYN_ENA and zeroed
GLTSYN_INCVAL on any port. ice_dev_stop() calls it for every port with
RTE_ETH_TX_OFFLOAD_SEND_ON_TIMESTAMP, so stopping a TxPP port on a
non-owning PF stopped the PHC of all sibling PFs and the clock under
the kernel's ptp4l. Only ice_ptp_init_phc() on the owner starts the
timer again, so the PHC stays stopped for every later process on the
device until the owner is initialized again.

ice_timesync_enable() also set the shared timer to CLOCK_REALTIME on
any port, on E830 with a direct GLTSYN_TIME write, which steps the PHC
under whoever owns it.

Stop the timer in ice_timesync_disable() only on the owner. In
ice_timesync_enable(), set the time only on the port that starts the
timer: the owner itself, or the owner port probed in this process. A
non-owning port leaves a running timer alone. Its timesync enable
before port start fails when the timer is stopped and its owner is
not probed in this process, instead of warning and reading 0.

This applies on top of MTL's patch 0007: the no-owner branch and the
time write through the owner port only exist there. The part for
upstream DPDK is the owner check in ice_timesync_disable() and the
time write only on the owner in ice_timesync_enable().

Fixes: 646dcbe6c701 ("net/ice: support IEEE 1588 PTP")
Fixes: faa310a75f66 ("net/ice: initialize PHC time with current time")
Fixes: 8d1dae92e9ca ("net/ice: fix PTP clock corruption with Tx packet pacing")

Signed-off-by: Andrzej Wilczynski <andrzej.wilczynski@intel.com>
---
 drivers/net/intel/ice/ice_ethdev.c | 48 +++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/intel/ice/ice_ethdev.c b/drivers/net/intel/ice/ice_ethdev.c
index 95bfc9b504..8c8659fbd4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/intel/ice/ice_ethdev.c
+++ b/drivers/net/intel/ice/ice_ethdev.c
@@ -7210,6 +7210,7 @@ ice_timesync_enable(struct rte_eth_dev *dev)
 	struct ice_hw *hw = ICE_DEV_PRIVATE_TO_HW(dev->data->dev_private);
 	struct ice_adapter *ad =
 			ICE_DEV_PRIVATE_TO_ADAPTER(dev->data->dev_private);
+	struct ice_hw *init_hw = NULL;
 	int ret;
 
 	if (ad->txpp_ena)
@@ -7234,6 +7235,7 @@ ice_timesync_enable(struct rte_eth_dev *dev)
 				"Failed to write PHC increment time value");
 			return -1;
 		}
+		init_hw = hw;
 	} else {
 		/*
 		 * This function does not own the shared source timer. Make
@@ -7248,11 +7250,15 @@ ice_timesync_enable(struct rte_eth_dev *dev)
 			ice_timesync_find_src_tmr_owner(dev);
 
 		if (!owner_dev) {
-			PMD_DRV_LOG(WARNING,
-				"PHC source timer owner port for %s is not probed in this process; "
-				"PHC reads on this port will return 0 unless the owner port is "
-				"also opened and timesync-enabled",
-				dev->data->name);
+			uint8_t tmr_idx = hw->func_caps.ts_func_info.tmr_index_assoc;
+
+			if (!(ICE_READ_REG(hw, GLTSYN_ENA(tmr_idx)) & GLTSYN_ENA_TSYN_ENA_M)) {
+				PMD_DRV_LOG(ERR,
+					"PHC source timer of %s is stopped and its owner port is "
+					"not probed in this process",
+					dev->data->name);
+				return -1;
+			}
 		} else {
 			struct ice_hw *owner_hw =
 				ICE_DEV_PRIVATE_TO_HW(owner_dev->data->dev_private);
@@ -7276,19 +7282,22 @@ ice_timesync_enable(struct rte_eth_dev *dev)
 						owner_dev->data->name);
 					return -1;
 				}
+				init_hw = owner_hw;
 			}
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (!ice_ptp_lock(hw)) {
-		ice_debug(hw, ICE_DBG_PTP, "Failed to acquire PTP semaphore");
-		return ICE_ERR_NOT_READY;
-	}
+	if (init_hw) {
+		if (!ice_ptp_lock(init_hw)) {
+			ice_debug(init_hw, ICE_DBG_PTP, "Failed to acquire PTP semaphore");
+			return ICE_ERR_NOT_READY;
+		}
 
-	ret = ice_ptp_write_init(hw);
-	ice_ptp_unlock(hw);
-	if (ret)
-		PMD_INIT_LOG(ERR, "Failed to set current system time to PHC timer");
+		ret = ice_ptp_write_init(init_hw);
+		ice_ptp_unlock(init_hw);
+		if (ret)
+			PMD_INIT_LOG(ERR, "Failed to set current system time to PHC timer");
+	}
 
 	ad->ptp_ena = 1;
 
@@ -7504,12 +7513,15 @@ ice_timesync_disable(struct rte_eth_dev *dev)
 
 	ice_clear_phy_tstamp(hw, lport, 0);
 
-	val = ICE_READ_REG(hw, GLTSYN_ENA(tmr_idx));
-	val &= ~GLTSYN_ENA_TSYN_ENA_M;
-	ICE_WRITE_REG(hw, GLTSYN_ENA(tmr_idx), val);
+	/* The source timer is shared by all ports; only its owner may stop it */
+	if (hw->func_caps.ts_func_info.src_tmr_owned) {
+		val = ICE_READ_REG(hw, GLTSYN_ENA(tmr_idx));
+		val &= ~GLTSYN_ENA_TSYN_ENA_M;
+		ICE_WRITE_REG(hw, GLTSYN_ENA(tmr_idx), val);
 
-	ICE_WRITE_REG(hw, GLTSYN_INCVAL_L(tmr_idx), 0);
-	ICE_WRITE_REG(hw, GLTSYN_INCVAL_H(tmr_idx), 0);
+		ICE_WRITE_REG(hw, GLTSYN_INCVAL_L(tmr_idx), 0);
+		ICE_WRITE_REG(hw, GLTSYN_INCVAL_H(tmr_idx), 0);
+	}
 
 	ad->ptp_ena = 0;
 
-- 
2.34.1

